# Form Engine — JSON-Driven Wizard

The entire loan application is rendered from a `LoanProduct` JSON config. **Never hardcode form fields.**

## Core Type Hierarchy

```
LoanProduct
└── templates: FormTemplate[]       ← each template = one wizard step
    └── sections: FormSection[]     ← each section = one Card
        └── fields: FormField[]     ← each field = one input
            └── validation: FieldValidation
```

## FormTemplate — Wizard Step Config

```ts
interface FormTemplate {
  code: string;         // unique key, used as formData key
  title: string;        // step label
  repeatable?: boolean; // true → user can add/remove instances (e.g. Owner Profile)
  minInstances?: number;
  maxInstances?: number;
  sections: FormSection[];
}
```

## FormSection — Card inside a Step

```ts
interface FormSection {
  code: string;
  title: string;
  repeatable?: boolean;   // section-level repeatable (e.g. multiple addresses)
  columns?: 1 | 2 | 3 | 4;
  fields: FormField[];
}
```

## FormField — Individual Input

```ts
interface FormField {
  name: string;
  label: string;
  type: FieldType;        // see supported types below
  placeholder?: string;
  options?: FieldOption[]; // for 'select' type
  validation?: FieldValidation;
  span?: 1 | 2 | 3 | 4 | 6 | 12; // grid column span
  accept?: string;        // for 'file' type (e.g. ".pdf,.jpg")
  maxFiles?: number;
  maxSize?: number;       // in MB
}
```

## Supported Field Types → Component Mapping

| `type` | Rendered as |
|--------|-------------|
| `text` | `<Input type="text">` |
| `textarea` | `<Textarea>` |
| `number` | `<Input type="number">` |
| `currency` | Formatted amount input (₹ prefix, grouping, fixed decimals) |
| `percentage` | Input with % suffix |
| `email` | `<Input type="email">` |
| `tel` | `<Input type="tel">` |
| `checkbox` | `<Checkbox>` |
| `select` | `<Select>` (Radix) |
| `multiselect` | Dropdown with selected values as removable chips. Payload is a string array. |
| `datetime` | `<Input type="date">` |
| `file` | `<FileUploadField>` (drag-drop) |
| `document` | Same as `file`. Also accepts a document-slot JSON shape (`documentType` + `upload`). |
| `json` | `<Textarea>` (raw JSON) |
| `address` | Composite group: Address Line 1, Address Line 2, City, State, PIN Code, Country. |

Configure it as a single field — the renderer expands the subfields automatically, and submitted data is nested under the field `name`:

```json
{
  "name": "address",
  "type": "address",
  "label": "Registered Address",
  "validation": { "required": true }
}
```

```ts
// payload
{
  address: {
    addressLine1: "42 MG Road",
    addressLine2: "Near City Center",
    city: "Mumbai",
    state: "Maharashtra",
    pincode: "400001",
    country: "India",
  }
}
```

## Validation Rules (Zod v3 generated dynamically)

```ts
interface FieldValidation {
  required?: boolean;
  maxLength?: number;
  minLength?: number;
  pattern?: string;       // regex string → z.string().regex(new RegExp(pattern))
  min?: number;
  max?: number;
  minExclusive?: number;  // z.number().gt()
  maxExclusive?: number;  // z.number().lt()
  integer?: boolean;      // z.number().int()
  email?: boolean;        // z.string().email()
  phone?: boolean;        // regex validation
  message?: string;       // custom error message
}
```

Length limits may also be authored under `constraints` (e.g. `{ "constraints": { "minLength": 11, "maxLength": 11 } }`) — they merge into `validation`.

Live typing rules are authored as `input` and applied while the user types (trim runs on blur):

```json
{
  "input": {
    "trim": true,
    "uppercase": true,
    "allowSpaces": false,
    "allowSpecialCharacters": false
  },
  "constraints": { "minLength": 11, "maxLength": 11 },
  "validation": { "pattern": "^[A-Z]{4}0[A-Z0-9]{6}$" }
}
```

`allowSpecialCharacters: false` keeps letters and digits, or digits only when `validation.pattern` is numeric (e.g. `^[0-9]+$`).

## Conditional visibility

A field can be shown only when a sibling field matches a condition. Both of these JSON shapes work:

```json
{ "visibleWhen": { "field": "loanPurpose", "equals": "OTHER" } }
```

```json
{
  "rules": {
    "visibleWhen": { "field": "loanPurpose", "operator": "equals", "value": "OTHER" }
  }
}
```

`requiredWhen` uses the same shapes. Hidden fields are skipped during validation.

## Currency formatting

`type: "currency"` always uses grouped, fixed-decimal input. Extra JSON keys are optional overrides (other field types ignore them):

```json
{
  "name": "loanAmount",
  "type": "currency",
  "label": "Loan Amount",
  "required": true,
  "min": 1,
  "max": 9999999999999999.99,
  "precision": 18,
  "scale": 2,
  "decimalScale": 2,
  "fixedDecimalScale": true,
  "thousandSeparator": ",",
  "decimalSeparator": ".",
  "allowNegative": false,
  "allowLeadingZeros": false,
  "useGrouping": true
}
```

The form stores a number (e.g. `1500000.50`); separators are display-only.

## Document uploads

A document slot can be authored without `name`/`type`. `documentType` becomes the field name, `type` defaults to `document`, and `upload` maps onto the existing file control:

```json
{
  "documentType": "OTHER",
  "label": "Other Supporting Documents",
  "description": "Upload any additional documents requested during the loan review process.",
  "required": false,
  "upload": {
    "allowedExtensions": ["pdf", "jpg", "jpeg", "png", "doc", "docx"],
    "maxFileSizeMB": 10,
    "minFiles": 0,
    "maxFiles": 10
  }
}
```

A JSON array of these slots renders as a Documents upload screen. Values are stored as `File[]` under `documentType`.

Schema is built in `src/utils/schema-builder.ts`:
- `buildFieldSchema(field)` → `z.ZodTypeAny`
- `buildSectionSchema(section)` → `z.ZodObject`
- `buildTemplateSchema(template)` → `z.ZodObject`

## Form Data Shape

State is stored in `useWizardStore` keyed by `templateCode`:

```ts
formData = {
  "BUSINESS_PROFILE": {         // templateCode
    "BUSINESS_DETAILS": { ... }, // sectionCode → field values
    "BUSINESS_ADDRESS": { ... },
  },
  "OWNER_PROFILE": [            // repeatable template → array
    { "OWNER_DETAILS": { ... } },
    { "OWNER_DETAILS": { ... } },
  ],
}
```

## Wizard Step Components

```
FormWizard        — top-level orchestrator; owns step state, navigation, save/submit
├── WizardProgress  — step indicator with completion dots
├── WizardStep      — renders a single FormTemplate
│   ├── SingleTemplateForm     — non-repeatable: FormProvider + DynamicSection[]
│   └── RepeatableTemplateInstances → RepeatableInstance[] (each has own useForm)
└── ReviewScreen    — shows all formData; edit buttons jump back to step
```

## Adding a New Wizard Step

1. Add a new `FormTemplate` object to `templates[]` in `src/services/mock-data.ts`.
2. No component changes needed — `FormWizard` iterates `product.templates` dynamically.

## Adding a New Field Type

1. Add the type string to `FieldType` union in `src/types/index.ts`.
2. Handle it in `DynamicField.tsx` (render the right component).
3. Handle it in `buildFieldSchema()` in `src/utils/schema-builder.ts` (Zod rule).

## Mock Data Location

`src/services/mock-data.ts` exports:
- `MOCK_USER` — demo user object
- `MOCK_APPLICATIONS` — 5 sample applications (draft/submitted/approved/rejected)
- `MOCK_SUMMARY` — dashboard counts
- `LOAN_FORM_TEMPLATES` — full 6-step `LoanProduct` for Business Loan
